Q: How to center an element in the middle of the browser window? A: <p>If you don't know the size of the browser you can simply center in CSS with the following code:</p>
<p>This also helps in any unforeseen changes in the future.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.firstDiv {
  width: 500px;

  position: fixed;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);

  background-color: #F1F1F1;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div class="firstDiv"&gt;Some Text&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
